Investigate this Wazuh alert:

{
  "severity": "high",
  "network_observations": [
    {"ip": "10.30.7.66", "inferred_role": "developer_workstation_resigning_employee", "first_seen": "2027-08-11T22:18:42+0200", "last_seen": "2027-08-11T23:18:42+0200", "agent_name": "LAPTOP-DEV-12"},
    {"ip": "drive.google.com", "inferred_role": "personal_cloud_storage_exfil_destination", "first_seen": "2027-08-11T22:42:18+0200", "last_seen": "2027-08-11T23:18:42+0200"}
  ],
  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Collection / Data Staging", "technique": "T1074.001 + T1213.003", "what_happened": "At 2027-08-11 22:18:42 CEST, Sysmon Event 1 fired on LAPTOP-DEV-12 (10.30.7.66): 'git.exe clone --depth=1 ssh://git@gitlab.corp.local/corp/monorepo.git C:\\Users\\samir.b\\Documents\\backup\\corp-code' with parentImage=bash.exe (WSL git wrapper) under user=CORP\\samir.b. The corp/monorepo is the company's FULL source-code repository (~4.8 GB) — cloning it in entirety to a personal staging folder ('Documents\\backup\\corp-code') is profoundly anomalous: developers normally pull branch-level updates or single-component clones, never the complete monorepo in one operation. The --depth=1 flag indicates the actor wants the latest snapshot only (smallest transfer footprint, fastest), which is the canonical exfil-optimised clone pattern. Naming the destination 'backup' is the classic insider-rationalisation pattern ('I just kept a backup').", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 1 (rule.id 61613, level 8): image=git.exe + commandLine contains 'clone' + commandLine contains 'monorepo.git' + user=CORP\\samir.b. The action was flagged because 'samir.b' is HRIS-marked 'RESIGNED, end-date 2027-08-25' = high-risk-window departing employee. Wazuh decoder cross-references Sysmon process create with HRIS-resigning-flag list to escalate.", "first_seen": "2027-08-11T22:18:42+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Collection / Local File System Activity", "technique": "T1074.001", "what_happened": "From 22:22:18 to 22:31:48 CEST, Sysmon Event 11 fired ~12,400 times on LAPTOP-DEV-12 — every File Create event lands under 'C:\\Users\\samir.b\\Documents\\backup\\corp-code\\' as git unpacks the monorepo to disk (source files, .git/objects, packfiles). The file-create rate is consistent with git clone unpacking a ~4.8 GB monorepo (~22 files/sec average). Total local stage size after clone = ~4.8 GB in a single user-profile subdirectory.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 11 burst on a single targetFilename path tree, single user, single parent process (git.exe). Diagnostic of bulk source-code staging, not normal developer workflow which produces scattered FCs across multiple repos + branch checkouts over time.", "first_seen": "2027-08-11T22:22:18+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Collection (Server-Side Audit)", "technique": "T1213.003", "what_happened": "At 22:28:42 CEST, GitLab audit log (forwarded to Wazuh via syslog) recorded: action='clone', user='samir.b', repo='corp/monorepo', size='4.8 GB', source_ip='10.30.7.66'. The Wazuh decoder enriched this event with HRIS context (samir.b RESIGNED flag) and fired a HIGH-level alert: 'Clone of high-value monorepo by HR-flagged departing employee'. The GitLab-side evidence corroborates the Sysmon-side evidence — the clone is real, server-confirmed, and the source code DID transit from the GitLab server to LAPTOP-DEV-12.", "chain_reason": "GitLab audit log + Wazuh HRIS-decoder cross-reference rule (rule.id 100412, level 12). Two-signal correlation: server-side clone event + HRIS-flagged user. The rule fires precisely on this combination, which is operationally rare for non-malicious workflows.", "first_seen": "2027-08-11T22:28:42+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Collection / Archive Collected Data", "technique": "T1560.001", "what_happened": "At 22:32:14 CEST, Sysmon Event 1 fired: '7z.exe a -t7z -mx=9 -p\"strong-pwd-2027\" C:\\Users\\samir.b\\Documents\\corp-code.7z C:\\Users\\samir.b\\Documents\\backup\\corp-code\\*' parentImage=explorer.exe under user=CORP\\samir.b. The flags: -t7z (7z format) + -mx=9 (maximum compression) + -p\"strong-pwd-2027\" (PASSWORD-PROTECTED + ENCRYPTED archive). Password-protected encrypted archive of the just-cloned monorepo is the canonical pre-exfil collection step — encryption (a) reduces detectability by DLP content-inspection tools (the encrypted .7z is opaque), and (b) makes recovery via legal request to the cloud provider operationally harder. Choice of explorer.exe parent indicates the actor double-clicked / right-clicked from File Explorer to launch 7z — a manual user action, not a scripted background process.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 1: image=7z.exe + commandLine contains '-p\"' (password flag) + commandLine contains 'corp-code' (target name) + parentImage=explorer.exe + user=CORP\\samir.b. The -p flag (password-protected encrypted archive) on a sensitive folder by a flagged-resigning user fires Wazuh rule.id 100413.", "first_seen": "2027-08-11T22:32:14+0200"},
    {"step": 5, "tactic": "Exfiltration / Network Connection", "technique": "T1567.002 + T1052.001", "what_happened": "From 22:42:18 CEST to 23:17:48 CEST (35 minutes), Sysmon Event 3 (Network Connection) fired repeatedly: image=chrome.exe initiating outbound HTTPS connections to drive.google.com:443 with cumulative transfer size 4.6 GB. The destination drive.google.com is the user's PERSONAL Google Drive account, NOT the corporate Google Workspace (the corp tenant is corp-onedrive.sharepoint.com / corp.onedrive.live + a separate corp-tenant Google Workspace, neither matches consumer drive.google.com). Personal-cloud upload of multi-gigabyte data from a corporate-managed laptop by a flagged-resigning user, with 4.6 GB ≈ the password-protected 7z size, is the diagnostic exfil signature.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 3 + Wazuh personal-cloud-domain enrichment list (drive.google.com, dropbox.com, mega.nz, wetransfer.com, sendgb.com, etc.). Wazuh rule.id 100414 fires when a corporate-managed agent uploads >100 MB to any domain in the personal-cloud list. 4.6 GB is well above threshold.", "first_seen": "2027-08-11T22:42:18+0200"},
    {"step": 6, "tactic": "Exfiltration (Web Proxy Confirmation)", "technique": "T1567.002", "what_happened": "At 22:48:42 CEST, Wazuh Web proxy log (syslog from corp-proxy-01) recorded: method='POST', url='drive.google.com/upload', user='samir.b' (LDAP-authenticated at proxy), size_uploaded='4.6 GB'. This is the corporate web-proxy's view of the same upload, cross-correlating with the Sysmon Event 3 endpoint-side evidence. The proxy log makes the user attribution unambiguous (LDAP-authenticated session, not just an IP). The bytes-uploaded value matches the local 7z archive size — high confidence that the encrypted source-code archive transited the corporate proxy to a personal cloud account.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh web-proxy decoder + personal-cloud-domain enrichment + LDAP-user enrichment. The 4.6 GB threshold + personal-cloud-destination + flagged-resigning user fires rule.id 100415 (level 13).", "first_seen": "2027-08-11T22:48:42+0200"},
    {"step": 7, "tactic": "Defense Evasion / Indicator Removal on Host", "technique": "T1070.004", "what_happened": "At 23:18:42 CEST (60 minutes after the original clone, immediately after exfil completed), Sysmon Event 1 fired: 'cmd.exe /c del /F /S /Q C:\\Users\\samir.b\\Documents\\backup\\corp-code\\*' parentImage=explorer.exe under user=CORP\\samir.b. The del /F /S /Q flags = Force + Subdirectories recursively + Quiet (no per-file confirmation). The actor is cleaning up the local clone directory post-exfil — the goal is to leave minimal forensic trace on the local disk in case the laptop is inspected after termination. Note: the original encrypted .7z archive (C:\\Users\\samir.b\\Documents\\corp-code.7z) is NOT in the deletion path = the actor kept the archive locally (or moved it elsewhere) but cleaned the unpacked source tree which is the bulkier and more incriminating artifact.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 1: image=cmd.exe + commandLine contains 'del /F /S /Q' + commandLine contains 'backup\\corp-code' + user=CORP\\samir.b. Recursive forced quiet deletion of just-staged data ≈ indicator removal on host. Fires Wazuh rule.id 100416 (level 10).", "first_seen": "2027-08-11T23:18:42+0200"}
  ],
  "time_window": {"start": "2027-08-11T22:18:42+0200", "end": "2027-08-11T23:18:42+0200"},
  "alert_count": 14,
  "unique_steps": 7
}
